6:8: warning: An `echo -e` relies on a bash builtin, the POSIX `echo` prints the flag as text.
     6 |    echo -e escaped
       |         ^~
note: Use `printf` instead under a `sh` shebang.
7:8: warning: An `echo -n` relies on a bash builtin, the POSIX `echo` prints the flag as text.
     7 |    echo -n nonewline
       |         ^~
note: Use `printf` instead under a `sh` shebang.
8:3: warning: The `declare` builtin is not in POSIX.
     8 |    declare -A assoc
       |    ^~~~~~~
note: Assign the variable plainly under a `sh` shebang, or switch the shebang to bash.
9:3: warning: The `typeset` builtin is not in POSIX.
     9 |    typeset scoped
       |    ^~~~~~~
note: Assign the variable plainly under a `sh` shebang, or switch the shebang to bash.
10:3: warning: The name `source` is the bash spelling, the POSIX dot command is `.`.
    10 |    source library.sh
       |    ^~~~~~
note: Use `.` under a `sh` shebang.
13:7: warning: The `<(...)` process substitution is a bash extension absent from POSIX sh.
    13 |    cat <(echo substituted)
       |        ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
note: Use a named pipe or a temporary file under a `sh` shebang.
14:8: warning: The extended glob `!(excluded)` is a bash extension absent from POSIX sh.
    14 |    echo !(excluded)
       |         ^~~~~~~~~~~
note: Use a `case` statement or a plain glob under a `sh` shebang.
15:8: warning: The `$'...'` quoting form is a bash extension absent from POSIX sh.
    15 |    echo $'a\tb'
       |         ^~~~~~~
note: Use `printf` to produce the escapes under a `sh` shebang.
16:8: warning: A `^` opens the bracket expression `[^a]tail` where POSIX sh negates with `!`.
    16 |    echo [^a]tail
       |         ^~~~~~~~
note: Use `[! ...]` under a `sh` shebang.
17:3: warning: An `echo` of a command substitution prints what the command already prints.
    17 |    echo "$(<file)"
       |    ^~~~
note: Run the command on its own instead.
17:9: warning: The `$(<file)` form is a bash shorthand absent from POSIX sh.
    17 |    echo "$(<file)"
       |          ^~~~~~~~
note: Use `$(cat file)` under a `sh` shebang.
18:3: warning: An `echo` of a command substitution prints what the command already prints.
    18 |    echo "`<file`"
       |    ^~~~
note: Run the command on its own instead.
18:9: warning: The `` `<file` `` form is a bash shorthand absent from POSIX sh.
    18 |    echo "`<file`"
       |          ^~~~~~~
note: Use `$(cat file)` under a `sh` shebang.
19:9: warning: The indirect expansion of `!indirect` is a bash extension absent from POSIX sh.
    19 |    echo "${!indirect}"
       |          ^~~~~~~~~~~~
note: Use `eval` or a `case` dispatch under a `sh` shebang.
20:9: warning: The array reference `array[0]` is a bash extension absent from POSIX sh.
    20 |    echo "${array[0]}"
       |          ^~~~~~~~~~~
note: Use the positional parameters under a `sh` shebang.
21:9: warning: The array key expansion of `!array[@]` is a bash extension absent from POSIX sh.
    21 |    echo "${!array[@]}"
       |          ^~~~~~~~~~~~
note: Use the positional parameters under a `sh` shebang.
22:9: warning: The name prefix expansion of `!prefix*` is a bash extension absent from POSIX sh.
    22 |    echo "${!prefix*}"
       |          ^~~~~~~~~~~
note: List the names explicitly under a `sh` shebang.
23:9: warning: The substring expansion of `text:1:2` is a bash extension absent from POSIX sh.
    23 |    echo "${text:1:2}"
       |          ^~~~~~~~~~~
note: Use `expr` or `cut` under a `sh` shebang.
24:9: warning: The string replacement in `text/from/to` is a bash extension absent from POSIX sh.
    24 |    echo "${text/from/to}"
       |          ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
note: Use `sed` or a `case` dispatch under a `sh` shebang.
25:9: warning: 'RANDOM' is a bash variable that POSIX sh leaves undefined.
    25 |    echo "$RANDOM"
       |          ^~~~~~~
note: Compute the value another way under a `sh` shebang.
30:15: warning: The `&>` redirection is a bash extension absent from POSIX sh.
    30 |    echo both &>out.log
       |                ^~~~~~~
note: Write the file redirect and `2>&1` separately under a `sh` shebang.
31:18: warning: The `&>` redirection is a bash extension absent from POSIX sh.
    31 |    echo append &>>out.log
       |                   ^~~~~~~
note: Write the file redirect and `2>&1` separately under a `sh` shebang.
32:14: warning: The `>&` redirection to 'outfile' is a bash extension absent from POSIX sh.
    32 |    echo dup >&outfile
       |               ^~~~~~~
note: Write the file redirect and `2>&1` separately under a `sh` shebang.
33:8: warning: The named file descriptor '{logfd}' is a bash extension absent from POSIX sh.
    33 |    exec {logfd}>trace.log
       |         ^~~~~~~
note: Name a fixed descriptor number under a `sh` shebang.
34:16: warning: The file descriptor '12' is outside the range POSIX sh defines.
    34 |    echo high 12>high.log
       |                 ^~~~~~~~
note: Use a descriptor from 0 to 9 under a `sh` shebang.
35:13: warning: The path '/dev/tcp/example.com/80' is a bash network device that POSIX sh leaves undefined.
    35 |    echo net >/dev/tcp/example.com/80
       |              ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
note: Open the connection with a network client under a `sh` shebang.
36:14: warning: The redirection target 'prefix*.log' is a glob that POSIX sh leaves undefined.
    36 |    echo glob >prefix*.log
       |               ^~~~~~~~~~~
note: Name the file explicitly under a `sh` shebang.
40:3: warning: The standalone `((...))` command is a bash extension absent from POSIX sh.
    40 |    ((counter + 1))
       |    ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
note: Use the `: $((...))` form under a `sh` shebang.
41:8: warning: The `++` operator in arithmetic is undefined in POSIX sh.
    41 |    : $((counter++))
       |         ^~~~~~~~~
note: Write the assignment out under a `sh` shebang.
42:8: warning: The `--` operator in arithmetic is undefined in POSIX sh.
    42 |    : $((counter--))
       |         ^~~~~~~~~
note: Write the assignment out under a `sh` shebang.
43:8: warning: The `**` operator in arithmetic is undefined in POSIX sh.
    43 |    : $((base ** exponent))
       |         ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
note: Multiply the value out under a `sh` shebang.
44:11: warning: The `<` comparison in `test` is undefined in POSIX sh.
    44 |    [ alpha \< beta ]
       |            ^~
note: Compare with `expr` or a `case` statement under a `sh` shebang.
45:11: warning: The `>` comparison in `test` is undefined in POSIX sh.
    45 |    [ alpha \> beta ]
       |            ^~
note: Compare with `expr` or a `case` statement under a `sh` shebang.
46:11: warning: The `-nt` operator in `test` is undefined in POSIX sh.
    46 |    [ first -nt second ]
       |            ^~~
note: Compare the timestamps with `find` or `ls` under a `sh` shebang.
47:11: warning: The `-ef` operator in `test` is undefined in POSIX sh.
    47 |    [ first -ef second ]
       |            ^~~
note: Compare the timestamps with `find` or `ls` under a `sh` shebang.
48:5: warning: The unary `-a` in `test` is undefined in POSIX sh.
    48 |    [ -a present ]
       |      ^~
note: Use `-e` instead.
49:11: warning: The literals 'alpha' and 'beta' differ, so the comparison never succeeds.
    49 |    [ alpha = beta ]
       |            ^
note: Compare a variable, or correct the operand spelling.
54:3: warning: The `time` keyword times only a simple command in POSIX sh.
    54 |    time { printf 'grouped\n'; }
       |    ^~~~
note: Run the compound command through `sh -c` and time that.
55:3: warning: The `time` keyword times only a simple command in POSIX sh.
    55 |    time ( printf 'subshell\n' )
       |    ^~~~
note: Run the compound command through `sh -c` and time that.
53:3: warning: The `time` keyword times only a simple command in POSIX sh.
    53 |    time printf 'timed\n' | wc -l
       |    ^~~~
note: Time one stage, or run the pipeline through `bash -c` and time that.
61:3: warning: Commands after `exec` do not run when `exec` succeeds.
    61 |    exec -c env
       |    ^~~~
62:3: details:
    62 |    let value=1
       |    ^~~~~~~~~~~ this is the first command skipped after `exec`.
note: Remove the `exec`, or remove the unreachable commands.
59:3: warning: The `+=` assignment to 'LIST' is a bash extension absent from POSIX sh.
    59 |    LIST+=extra
       |    ^~~~~~~~~~~
note: Write `NAME="$NAME"value` under a `sh` shebang.
60:3: warning: The `+=` assignment to 'PREFIX' is a bash extension absent from POSIX sh.
    60 |    PREFIX+=extra env
       |    ^~~~~~~~~~~~~
note: Write `NAME="$NAME"value` under a `sh` shebang.
61:8: warning: The `exec` `-c` flag is a bash extension absent from POSIX sh.
    61 |    exec -c env
       |         ^~
note: Drop the flag under a `sh` shebang.
62:3: warning: The `let` builtin is a bash extension absent from POSIX sh.
    62 |    let value=1
       |    ^~~
note: Use the `: $((...))` form under a `sh` shebang.
63:18: warning: The `ERR` condition is a bash extension absent from POSIX sh.
    63 |    trap 'cleanup' ERR
       |                   ^~~
note: Check the status after each command under a `sh` shebang.
64:18: warning: The `SIG` prefix on 'SIGINT' is undefined in POSIX sh.
    64 |    trap 'cleanup' SIGINT
       |                   ^~~~~~
note: Name the signal without the `SIG` prefix under a `sh` shebang.
65:18: warning: The signal name 'int' is undefined in POSIX sh because it is not uppercase.
    65 |    trap 'cleanup' int
       |                   ^~~
note: Name the signal in uppercase under a `sh` shebang.
68:10: warning: The `printf` `%q` directive is a bash extension absent from POSIX sh.
    68 |    printf '%q\n' "$value"
       |           ^~~~~~
note: Quote the value another way under a `sh` shebang.
70:16: warning: The POSIX `.` command reads a file and takes no argument, so 'extra' never reaches it.
    70 |    . library.sh extra
       |                 ^~~~~
note: Set the values as variables before the file is read.
74:3: warning: The `$0` parameter cannot be assigned in POSIX sh, so '$0=zero' runs as a command.
